2:T62e,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a free AI study timetable generator?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. PlanBot offers free tools like the Daily Schedule Generator and Exam Revision Calculator that create a personalized study timetable in under a minute - no signup or payment required. The PlanBot app then automates the same process daily with AI."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I make a study timetable online?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"List your subjects, count the days until your exam, and divide hours by priority - weak subjects get more blocks. An AI timetable generator does this split for you automatically and rebalances it when you fall behind."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the best timetable for studying 10 hours a day?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Split 10 hours into 4-5 blocks of 2-2.5 hours with 15-30 minute breaks, place your hardest subject in your sharpest window (usually morning), keep one lighter revision block after lunch, and stop planning 30 minutes before sleep. A generator can arrange subjects into these blocks for you."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can AI create a study plan for competitive exams like JEE or NEET?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. AI planners build complete exam plans - subject rotation, revision cycles, and mock test scheduling. PlanBot includes dedicated workflows for JEE, NEET, CAT, UPSC and other exams, and adapts the plan daily based on what you actually complete."}}]}3:T4c4,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"Free AI Study Timetable Generator (No Signup)","description":"Generate a personalized study timetable online in under a minute. Free AI timetable maker for school and competitive exam students - no signup, just answer 3 questions and get your daily schedule.","step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"List your subjects and chapters","text":"Write down every subject you need to study, and mark which chapters or topics are weakest - the generator needs real inputs to make a real plan."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Set your exam date and available hours","text":"Enter when your exam is and how many hours you can realistically study each day. Be honest: a plan built on 10 imaginary hours collapses in 2 days."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Generate and review the split","text":"The tool divides your remaining days across subjects, weighting weak topics heavier and reserving final days for full revision and mocks."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Follow or automate it","text":"Use the timetable manually, or let an AI planner like PlanBot regenerate and adjust it every day automatically as you progress."}]}b:["slug","free-ai-study-timetable-generator","d"]
