4:[["$","div",null,{"className":"aeo-answer tl-dr","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Quick Answer:"}]," A free AI study timetable generator turns three inputs - your subjects, your exam date, and your daily available hours - into a weighted daily schedule in under a minute. Weak subjects get more time, finished days get revision blocks, and you never touch a spreadsheet. You can generate one right now using PlanBot's free ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/tools/daily-schedule-generator","children":"Daily Schedule Generator"}]," or ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/tools/exam-revision-calculator","children":"Exam Revision Calculator"}],", no signup needed."]}]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"What Is an AI Study Timetable Generator?"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"An AI study timetable generator is a tool that builds your daily or weekly study schedule automatically. Instead of you staring at a blank template wondering whether Physics should come before Chemistry, the generator does the arithmetic and the prioritization for you:"}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["It counts the ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"real days left"}]," before your exam"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["It splits those days across your ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"subjects and chapters"}]]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["It gives ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"more blocks to weak subjects"}]," without starving the strong ones"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["It reserves the ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"final stretch for revision and mock tests"}],", not new chapters"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["It arranges everything into ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"realistic daily blocks"}]," with breaks"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"The \"AI\" part matters at the adjustment step. A paper template is frozen the moment you print it. A generated schedule can be regenerated the next morning based on what you actually finished - which is the difference between a timetable that survives 10 months of preparation and one you abandon by Thursday."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"How to Generate Your Study Timetable in Under a Minute"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"You can do this with pen and paper, but here is the workflow generators automate:"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Step 1: List your subjects and mark your weak ones."}]," Not all subjects are equal. If Organic Chemistry is your disaster zone and you are scoring 80% in Maths already, equal time splits are quietly failing you."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Step 2: Enter your exam date and honest daily hours."}]," The single biggest planning mistake is building a timetable around 10 hours a day when you historically do 5. Plan for the hours you will actually do."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Step 3: Let the tool divide the days."}]," Topics you flagged weak get double weight. The last 15-20% of your timeline gets reserved for full syllabus revision and mock tests."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Step 4: Review the output against your reality."}]," If the plan says 3 hours of Maths in the morning but you have school till 4 PM, shift the block. Generators give structure; you give local knowledge."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Step 5: Follow it for 3 days, then regenerate."}]," Three days of real data (what got done, what slipped) is enough to rebalance everything. This is exactly what ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/blog/how-planbot-ai-works","children":"PlanBot's AI does automatically every morning"}]," - but manually regenerating with a free tool works too."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"What a Good Generated Timetable Looks Like"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Here is a real example for a Class 12 student with a Maths exam in 20 days, studying 6 hours daily:"}],"\n",["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Time block"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Duration"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"What goes here"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Why"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"6:00 - 8:30 AM"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"2.5 h"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Calculus (weak topic)"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Sharpest focus window goes to the weakest subject"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"8:30 - 9:00 AM"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"30 min"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Breakfast / walk"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Real break, not \"quick scroll\" that eats an hour"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"9:00 - 11:00 AM"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"2 h"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Vectors & 3D Geometry"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Second-priority topic while energy is still high"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"4:00 - 5:30 PM"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"1.5 h"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Previous year questions"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Active recall beats re-reading in the afternoon slump"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"7:00 - 8:00 PM"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"1 h"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Formula revision (spaced)"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"End-of-day review locks the morning's work"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"8:00 - 8:30 PM"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"30 min"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Next-day mini plan"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Closing the loop - what slipped moves to tomorrow"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Total: 7 hours of plan, 6 hours realistic after breaks. Notice what the table does NOT contain: 12-hour fantasy days, subjects scheduled into slots you know you will sleep through, or new chapters in the final week. That discipline is what generators enforce and self-made timetables abandon."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Why Free Timetable Templates Keep Failing You"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"If you have ever downloaded a \"topper timetable PDF\" and quit it within a week, the template was not the problem. Three structural reasons static timetables fail:"}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"They are built for an imaginary student."}]," Someone else's school timing, energy curve, and subject strengths got baked in. Your timetable needs your inputs - which is what a generator asks for."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"They cannot rebalance."}]," Miss one day of a rigid template and the whole week is out of sync. A generated plan absorbs the miss and re-splits the remaining days."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"They optimize for looks, not behavior."}]," Color-coded perfection feels productive but encodes nothing about priority. A generated timetable is weighted by weakness and exam distance - the two variables that actually matter."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Free Tools You Can Use Right Now (No Signup)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"You do not need to install anything to get your first timetable today. Each of these runs free in your browser:"}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/tools/daily-schedule-generator","children":"Daily Schedule Generator"}]}]," - builds an hour-by-hour day plan from your task list and available hours. Best for \"what do I do today?\""]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/tools/exam-revision-calculator","children":"Exam Revision Calculator"}]}]," - takes your exam date, subjects, and weak chapters, then splits your remaining days with revision built in. Best for \"how do I cover everything in time?\""]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/tools/pomodoro-focus-calculator","children":"Pomodoro Focus Calculator"}]}]," - converts your planned hours into focus-session blocks with break timing. Best if you lose focus mid-session."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["The catch with free tools: they generate a plan once, but ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"they cannot watch you execute it"}],". When you skip Tuesday's Physics block, no free calculator rearranges Wednesday for you."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Where AI Automation Takes Over from Generation"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Generation is one snapshot; real preparation is a movie. This is the gap between a free generator and an AI planner like PlanBot:"}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Daily regeneration:"}]," every morning the plan is rebuilt around what you actually completed - no manual rebalancing"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Weak-subject tracking:"}]," log a bad chapter and the AI automatically gives it heavier blocks in the coming days"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Spaced revision scheduling:"}]," completed topics reappear for review exactly when you are about to forget them"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Energy-aware placement:"}]," your hardest subjects land in your personal high-focus windows, learned from your own completion patterns"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["For students who want the automated version, ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=cpm.planbot","children":"PlanBot is free to download"}]," and generates this kind of adaptive schedule every day - the free web tools remain here whenever you just need a quick plan."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"children":"Start With the Plan, Not the Perfect Plan"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"The students who score highest are rarely the ones with the most beautiful timetable. They are the ones whose timetable was still alive in the final month. Generate one today - with whatever tool you like - and let it adjust as you go. That one habit outperforms every perfect plan you abandon."}],"\n",["$","hr",null,{}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["$","em",null,{"children":["Want the timetable to build and adjust itself every morning? ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=cpm.planbot","children":"Download PlanBot free on Android"}]," - AI daily planning for students and professionals."]}]}]]
